replace("The two experiment campaigns establish actual native and queue capability, including partial outcomes. They also expose discrepancies in CI scheduling, approval retention, signing and completed-group continuation.", "The original experiments and the November 8–9 follow-up establish actual native and queue capability, including partial outcomes. The follow-up changes the earlier method-only queue conclusion, verifies four website rebases, exercises genuine missing acknowledgements, and exposes recovery-prototype failures. CI scheduling, approval retention, signing and completed-group continuation still depend on the tested path and policy.")
replace("A local record can coordinate cooperating processes in that checkout.", "Cooperating processes in that checkout need one actual local owner across admission and dispatch. Each process must reload the current operation under that owner before sending an effect; cached admission and a lock-shaped record are insufficient. The same boundary must apply to direct worker, recovery and transfer entry paths.")
replace("If pending evidence is missing, enter recovery and withhold new mutation authority.", "If pending evidence is missing or names a different operation, enter recovery and withhold new mutation authority. Do not reconstruct fresh intent from command arguments. Recovery and transfer must also validate the accepted result claimed by a completed record: its retained objects, continuation and checkpoint, or an explicitly recorded legitimate successor. A completion flag alone grants no authority. Continued authoring may move the active branch; it must retain the accepted result and the evidence connecting it to that successor.")
replace("Other actors' permissions, discovery in a long discussion, reviewer comprehension and genuinely unknown comment writes remain untested.", "Follow-up tests establish actual distinct-actor permissions, programmed interleaving and duplicate-marker conflict handling. A privileged bot could edit a user-authored comment, so visible authorship is not exclusive edit authority. Genuine no-HTTP-read comment creation also produced its exact fresh comment. These observations do not provide general deduplication, ownership from a marker, or safe unknown-create replay. An informed browser agent reached the exact old patch and the labeled tip comparison; discovery in a long discussion and human comprehension remain untested.")
replace("Distinguish known-not-sent, rejected, acknowledged and indeterminate effects.", "Distinguish known-not-sent, definitely rejected, acknowledged and indeterminate effects. A received response is evidence of what it actually establishes: a timeout or server-error response may coexist with a completed mutation. Direct native group creations returned HTTP504 and502 while producing the intended99- and100-member groups. Preserve those writes as unknown until justified reconciliation; do not classify every error status as a no-effect rejection.")
