replace("The real-Git prototype exercised this algorithm through repeated import, ordinary Git rewrites, retained local amendments and conflicts, with 122 checks in its final local run.", "The real-Git prototype exercised this algorithm through repeated import, ordinary Git rewrites, retained local amendments and conflicts, with122 baseline assertions and broader follow-up checks across changing parents, modes, renames, deletion and binary content. Multi-commit tests preserve a flattened net range and its tip message, not every intermediate commit or message.")
replace("This sequence is useful client evidence, not a server transaction or a proof that every lifecycle race is safe.", "Nine follow-up fixtures resumed this sequence after actual SIGKILL and fresh-process recovery at acknowledged durable prefixes, including inserted-PR creation and completed registration. They preserved canonical PRs and exact archives without repeating completed effects. Missing-receipt and stale-head controls refused. These are after-ack recoveries; separate transport experiments cover genuinely unacknowledged writes. The sequence remains client evidence, not a server transaction or proof that every lifecycle race is safe.")
replace("Identity, updates, exact ranges, bounded size handling and programmed body/comment concurrency have evidence. Human discovery/comprehension, other roles and unknown-write recovery still need validation.", "Identity, updates, exact ranges, bounded size handling, distinct-actor permissions and programmed body/comment concurrency have evidence. An informed browser walkthrough verified the rendered links. Human discovery/comprehension and production unknown-write recovery still need validation; comment author identity does not enforce exclusive editing.")
replace("Before enrollment, establish an eligible required-check path for every layer's first publication and adoption, plus `merge_group` coverage.", "Before enrollment, establish an eligible required-check path for every layer's first publication and adoption, plus `merge_group` coverage. Follow-up fixtures supplied real push-event checks and a positive stacked target-workflow route after installing its required default-branch definition. Check context, SHA and producer identity all mattered. Actual CodeQL needed a fresh analysis after a native rewrite; deployment success on either tested source or candidate behaved differently from ordinary status-context precedence. Validate each actual rule path rather than deriving readiness from one generic green flag.")
